
`native/` holds the AUnit tests for ImplementSprayer/InterfaceSprayer
(../lib/SpuitcomputerSpCore/src/), run natively (no Teensy attached):

- `native/tests/` -- one `test_<ClassName>.cpp` per class under test.
- `native/support/` -- a small, self-contained set of Arduino-shaped stubs
  (Print/Stream/EEPROM/Arduino.h/etc.), not a real EpoxyDuino dependency, plus
  `native_main.cpp` (the host `int main()` entry point).
- `native/SpuitcomputerSpNativeTests.cpp` -- the single AUnit driver
  (`setup()`/`loop()`), matching Ploegbesturing's/Pootmachinebesturing's
  `PloegbesturingNativeTests.cpp`/`PootmachinebesturingNativeTests.cpp`
  pattern. Every `test_*.cpp` file only registers `test(...)` blocks; none of
  them define `setup()`/`loop()` themselves, so they all link into one
  combined binary instead of one binary per test file.
- `native/run_tests_msvc.ps1` -- MSVC fallback for Windows without GCC.

```
pio run -e native
.pio/build/native/program(.exe)
```

Needs a real host C++17 compiler on PATH (g++ or clang++) -- on Windows
without one, use test\native\run_tests_msvc.ps1 instead, which builds and
runs the same combined binary via MSVC directly. That script passes
`/Zc:preprocessor` -- MSVC's legacy preprocessor mishandles AUnit's
`test(SuiteName, testName)` argument-count dispatch, which every test in
this project uses (matching Ploegbesturing's/Pootmachinebesturing's
convention: groups each test's display name under the class it exercises,
e.g. `ImplementSprayer_dose_defaultsTo200`,
`InterfaceSprayer_update_allConditionsGood_selectsAuto`).

## Known gaps

- `CalibrationSprayer` (the LCD/button calibration wizard extracted from the
  legacy `InterfaceSprayer::calibrate()`) is `#ifdef ARDUINO`-guarded and
  deliberately excluded from `[env:native]`'s `build_src_filter` -- it drives
  real LCD/button hardware through a sequence of blocking `while(true)` nested
  menu loops, the same shape of problem Ploegbesturing's `CalibrationPlough`
  and Pootmachinebesturing's `CalibrationPlanter` have, and which is excluded
  there for the same reason. No native coverage exists or is planned for it.
- `ImplementSprayer::calculateSetpointPwm()`'s divide-by-zero guard (two
  calibration points capturing the same flow-pulse count) has no public
  setter to construct that state directly, unlike Plough's/Planter's position
  calibration -- `pwmCalibrationData` is only ever populated by
  `CalibratePump()` (a real, 60-second-real-time automated 12-point capture)
  or `readCalibrationData()`. The corrupt-EEPROM test exercises the
  validation path that keeps that state from ever being reached in practice,
  but the guard itself is untested in isolation.
- `InterfaceSprayer::UpdateScreen()` (LCD rendering) compiles as part of
  `InterfaceSprayer.cpp` (needed since `CheckButtons()`/`Update()`, which
  *are* tested, live in the same file) but its output isn't asserted on by
  any test -- `test/native/support/InterfaceI2CLCD.hpp`'s `WriteBuffer`/
  `WriteScreen` are no-ops.
- The `teensy41` real-board env has not been build-verified on real hardware
  -- only via `pio run -e teensy41`'s cross-compile in this environment.
- Only the `teensy41` board is wired up today. This module's legacy source
  also referenced a production Arduino Micro board, an Arduino Micro
  "voorserie" preseries board, and a Teensy 3.5/3.6 protoboard
  (`TEENSYPROTO`, including a remote pump-selection-over-`Serial1` protocol)
  -- their `#ifdef` branches remain in `ConfigSprayer.hpp`/
  `ConfigImplementSprayer.hpp`/`ConfigInterfaceSprayer.hpp` for future
  revival, but none of them has a buildable `platformio.ini` env yet.
- GPS-speed dosing is out of scope for this pass -- the legacy GPS
  constructor was a never-implemented stub, dropped entirely rather than
  carried forward. See `ImplementSprayer.hpp`'s note on wiring up real
  GPS-speed dosing later, mirroring Spuitcomputer LD's `ImplementSprayer`.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing (not used here -- pio test's
own Unity-based runner doesn't understand this project's AUnit setup):
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
